Patch 0091: new recompiler option general.emit_module_abi (off by default) for the game module.
What: with `emit_module_abi = true` in the TOML [general] table, every emitted .cpp and the two declaration headers
(ps2_recompiled_functions.h, ps2_recompiled_stubs.h) include only the module ABI headers of this repository
(don_guest_abi.h, don_guest_decls.h, don_guest_stubs.h under src/game_module/) instead of ps2_runtime.h, ps2_stubs.h,
ps2_syscalls.h, ps2_log.h, ps2_runtime_macros.h and <stdexcept>. The module build then needs no shim folder.
With the option off (the default) the output is byte-identical to before. Touches code_generator.h too (the flag
reaches the emitters through CodeGenerator).
Verified (T-614): built ps2_recomp from a scratch tree with patches 0001-0091; the frozen config with the option off
regenerates a tree with no differences from generated/ (diff -rq prints nothing); with it on, the includes are the ABI ones.
Not based on another project's code.

